[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125315,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 92,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Uveal melanocytoma is a subtype of uveal melanocytic naevus, comprising plump polygonal cells with dense intracytoplasmic melanin.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:20:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125316,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 92,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8726/0 Uveal melanocytoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:20:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125317,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 92,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F36.0 Benign neoplasm of choroid</p>\r\n<p>2F36.1 Benign neoplasm of iris</p>\r\n<p>2F36.2 Benign neoplasm of ciliary body</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:20:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125318,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 92,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> magnocellular naevus of the uvea.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:20:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125319,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 92,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:20:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125320,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 92,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Melanocytomas occur more frequently in the iris {15767055; 20829742} and ciliary body {10768345} than in the choroid; they are also found adjacent to the optic nerve head {20829742; 16500211}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:20:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125321,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 92,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "<p>Patients typically present with an asymptomatic discoid or dome-shaped dark-grey to black mass that elevates the retina, that can have a mossy or irregular surface that may cause iris heterochromia. Both ciliary body and iris melanocytomas can cause glaucoma. In a few cases, overlying orange pigment and subretinal fluid might be seen, which makes the distinction from a choroidal melanoma or other deeply pigmented choroidal naevi difficult {19125075; 11786063; 17621182; 32273508}.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>Imaging techniques of value include high-frequency anterior segment ultrasound biomicroscopy, ultrasound biomicroscopy, and B-scan ultrasonography. In uncertain cases, FNAB may be required {19125075}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:20:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125322,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 92,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Uveal melanocytomas are rare. The age at presentation ranges from infancy to 90&nbsp;years {902779; 17621182}. The distribution between the sexes and different ethnic groups is nearly equal {19125075}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:20:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125323,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 92,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:20:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125324,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 92,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Uveal melanocytomas harbour <em>GNAQ</em> mutations at exon&nbsp;5, <em>GNAQ</em> p.Q209L {23685997; 27239460}, with no other aberrations detected {23685997; 27239460; 35835335; 15767481}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:20:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125325,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 92,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>On gross examination, melanocytomas appear dark brown to jet back and generally measure 1&ndash;5&nbsp;mm in thickness.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:20:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125326,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 92,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "<p>Melanocytomas are composed of large polygonal pigmented melanocytes. Bleaching is usually required to adequately evaluate the tumour cells, which show a low N:C&nbsp;ratio and oval to round bland nuclei with inconspicuous nucleoli. Although necrosis can occur in large tumours, mitoses are frequently absent.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>Melanocytomas are positive for melan-A, HMB45, SOX10, MITF, and S100. Nuclear BAP1 immunoreactivity is retained. The Ki-67 growth fraction is very low or absent (0&ndash;2%) {11942551}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>The major differential diagnoses include uveal naevi and melanoma. Although uncommon, adenomas of the pigment epithelium of the ciliary body, iris, and/or retinal pigment epithelium should also be considered.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:21:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125327,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 92,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Uveal melanocytoma has large, ovoid cells with small, centrally located nuclei and pigmented cytoplasm {18323281}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:20:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 776,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125328,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 92,
        "headingId": 776,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:20:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 836,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 779,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125329,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 92,
        "headingId": 779,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a deeply pigmented uveal lesion with ovoid cells with abundant cytoplasm, small and centrally located nuclei, and few indistinct nucleoli.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> immunohistochemical confirmation of melanocytic lineage.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:20:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 834,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 777,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125330,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 92,
        "headingId": 777,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:20:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 835,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 778,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125331,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 92,
        "headingId": 778,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Instances of malignant transformation to melanoma are rare {1078332; 8010703; 23685997; 15965181}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:20:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]